  "title": "Qt: Check Flow Graph \"Limit to Display Filter\" in constructor",
  "description": "The documentation for the Flow Graph claims that the checkbox\nwill be checked if the main display filter is active before the\nwindow is opened. Make that actually the case, since most other\ndialogs do that. (See #19054.)\n\nConnect the displayFilterCheckBox toggled signal manually afterwards,\nso that an extra tap isn't triggered by enabling it in the constructor.",
